course: dictionary
lesson: 15608
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Tapped is the past tense of tap. It tells you that something happened already: «She tapped on the door.» Tap, taps and tapping are the same word in other forms.
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, so context matters. «She tapped on the window to get the cat's attention.» Tapped means hit something lightly and quickly. The clue is that it was a little knock, not a loud bang.
explain: Now read this: «He tapped the screen to open the game.» Here tapped means touched a screen with a finger. Look at the words around it: a screen, not a window, changes the meaning.
fact: Tap means hit something lightly and quickly.
fact: On phones and tablets, «tapped» means touched a screen or button with a finger.
fact: «Tapped into» means used something useful, such as water, energy or talent.
fact: Farmers and scientists can tap a maple tree, which means drawing out its sap.
fact: «Tapped out» is slang for having no money left or being very tired.
exercise: «She tapped on the door before she came in.» What does tapped mean here? | Broke into pieces | *Hit lightly and quickly | Painted over | Shouted loudly
exercise: «He tapped the icon, and the app opened.» What does tapped mean? | Ate it quickly | Hit it hard with a stick | *Touched it with a finger | Threw it away
exercise: «After the long trip, we were tapped out.» Which meaning fits best? | *Very tired, with no energy left | Full of food and happy | Bouncing with energy | Covered in paint
test: «The scientists tapped water from the rock below the ground.» What does tapped mean? | Drank it all at once | Painted over it | Hit it hard | *Drew out and used
test: «Someone secretly tapped the phone line.» Tapped means | Played loudly | Cut through | *Listened in secretly | Repaired
exam: «The farmer tapped the maple tree, and sap dripped into the bucket.» What did the farmer do to the tree? | Shook its leaves | Hit its bark with a hammer | Painted its bark | *Drew out its sap
